#: ../../source/docs/drivecalculator-guide.rst:5
#: 140b33d37a5a48459e86cb1f83447e83
msgid "DriveCalculator Motor and Prop Efficiency Guide"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/drivecalculator-guide.rst:7
#: a64091fb2e964b449c3ac91369ba70a7
msgid "`Drive Calculator <http://www.drivecalc.de>`__ is a free tool for brushless motor power system analysis and prop/motor selection. It has a large and growing database of motors, propellers, escs, and batteries. You can test combinations to get an estimate of maximum current, efficiency, prop speed, etc. It is available for Windows, MAC, and Linux."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/drivecalculator-guide.rst:9
#: b74f8ac57d834f70bc9a13fc1ae5dc2d
msgid "The screenshot below illustrates its interface and use. In this example, it shows an analysis of one of the motors used in the :ref:`MiniTalon Build example<miniTalon-build>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/drivecalculator-guide.rst:17
#: c8a13d3076f44f6187de73ddb3a8fb68
msgid "Entering the information"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/drivecalculator-guide.rst:19
#: 4cde0b7d83244f98b57f961c4d1b5656
msgid "After opening the application, you can select {1} the exact battery to be used,or the voltage to run the analysis, {2} the motor from a large database of motors/test data, and {3} the propeller to be used, again from a large database included. You can also change the ESC used {4}, although it will only make a minor difference in the analysis. It is shown, since that ESC was used to gather the motor test data entered into the database."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/drivecalculator-guide.rst:22
#: 6b4ef28c6c7845ee8ae7bd8d435c2e19
msgid "Results"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/drivecalculator-guide.rst:24
#: 2db0aa8e26224e9693a3876aff9dc61a
msgid "Instantly, the full throttle analysis will appear. {5} is the current at full throttle, {6} shows curves of efficiency versus throttle for the motor with that voltage source/battery. Static thrust and static propeller speed are shown in {7}. By scrolling through propellers in the list, you can instantly see the effects on the results. Likewise, you can choose and \"HOLD\" a voltage/battery, and/or propeller, and see the results as you scroll through motors in the database. You can also search for a motor's KV, weight, etc. and restrict the motors list to scroll through to only match those criteria."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/drivecalculator-guide.rst:27
#: 5099efb33446472fb399f654b19cec18
msgid "While not exact, due to component variations, etc. the results are very close to actual."
msgstr ""
